{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1516188-deviant-infused-with-mana-energy","id":1516188,"title":"Deviant infused with mana energy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T02:05:46-07:00","id":1516188,"title":"Deviant infused with mana energy","content":"Coactive are infused with an energy type, right? Or at least they certainly can be. And Mana is a type of energy. So a deviant infused with Mana? What would that be like? They wouldn't be a mage proper, but Mana manifests as a huge number of powers for mages. But for a devisnt? What kind of scars and variations could they get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10150-bob275","name":"bob275","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T02:19:34-07:00","id":1516189,"title":"","content":"You can give them a single &quot;spell&quot; equivalent (that is, model a power based on one of the core book's pre-made spells) while also giving them a Mana dependence. Make them a Thaumavore, basically. A Mana-vampire. The easiest starting spell would thus be something like <u>Devouring The Slain</u>, where you can do damage to others to gain Mana, or <u>Channel Mana</u> to just focus on sapping a Mage or their Hallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T02:42:49-07:00","id":1516190,"title":"","content":"Something to mimic Pattern Restoration.<br /> <br /> Something to mimic Pattern Scouring.<br /> <br /> Something to emulate Oblations.<br /> <br /> Something to subdue uncontrolled surges of power (in lieu of Mana mitigating Paradox).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T21:13:55-07:00","id":1524122,"title":"","content":"This depends on whether you want a generic mage or a Mage: the Awakening, 2nd edition mage. For a generic mage the following scars could function as either a mana pool or Vancian spellcasting: Concentration, Depletion, Involuntary Stimulus (set to use the Hybrid to supress all of the &quot;mage's&quot; powers), Power Failure, or Preparation. If you are going for blue book Mage, then I would say first check out Proximi/Proximus, their special rules for paradox, blessings, and their curse serve as excellent guidance for porting over to Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}